where
\eqn{(\alpha)_r = \frac{\Gamma(\alpha+r)}{\Gamma(\alpha)}},
and \eqn{a_x > 0}, \eqn{k > 0}, and \eqn{\rho > 0}.

When \eqn{\rho > 1}, the mean is:
\deqn{
E[Y] = \frac{a_x k}{\rho - 1}.
}

Therefore, the distribution can be parameterized in terms of its mean using:
\deqn{
a_x = \frac{\mu(\rho - 1)}{k}.
}

